      "answer": "**Study Guide: Pump Operation Procedure**\n=====================================\n\n### Part 1: Inspection\n\nBefore starting the pump, inspect the inlet for debris and check that the pressure gauge reads zero.\n\n**Practice Question:** What is the purpose of inspecting the inlet for debris?\n\n### Part 2: Operation\n\n1. Open the inlet valve before starting the pump.\n2. Start the pump and monitor the pressure gauge.\n3. Stop the pump if pressure exceeds 90 kPa.\n\n**Practice Question:** What is the maximum allowed pressure during pump operation?\n\n### Part 3: Shutdown\n\n1. Turn the motor off.\n2. Close the inlet valve.\n3. Record the final pressure.\n4. Do not open the casing while the pump is pressurized.\n\n**Short Answer Key:**\n\n1. What is the purpose of inspecting the inlet for debris?\nAnswer: [SOURCE_4aa01ffaff36f2799a03acb4] to ensure the inlet is clear of debris and the pressure gauge reads zero.\n2. What is the maximum allowed pressure during pump operation?\nAnswer: 90 kPa.\n3. What should not be done during shutdown?\nAnswer: Open the casing while the pump is pressurized.\n\n> Coverage check: 2 of 3 source sections have no linked substantive passage in this answer. The response may be incomplete; full coverage is not verified.",
